  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument now in No. 00-6567, Larry Dean Dusenbery v. the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The -- the Government argues that its 1988 procedures satisfied due process whether or not the notice was received."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court Record",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Federal Government forfeited Mr. Dusenbery's $22,000 in 1988 after mailing a notice to him at the Federal prison where he was incarcerated."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, you take the position that it's not sufficient that there be staff at the prison who deliver mail to the inmates?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, we've never required actual notice in any case, have we?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The 1988 procedures did not provide assurances of delivery because what happened after the mail reached the mail room is -- was vague and undocumented."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ZIEVE",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, but the reason that I emphasize the signature is because, as the Bureau of Prisons has since recognized, the -- the signature does help to improve delivery. It helps to make sure that this letter is treated with some extra attention and care. It ensures that it's not going to get misdelivered to Larry Smith two cells over."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ZIEVE",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They have to be adequate. My view is that under this Court's -- the analysis that this Court has used in its cases, in its due process cases, that applying that general statement leads to the same result that I'm arguing for here, although if the Court --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. ZIEVE",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the record, such as they are -- those procedures were inadequate. It's uncontested that he didn't get the notice, and the procedures as described, are inadequate, although for the same reasons as I think lead to actual notice, even if you don't want to go that far."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF JEFFREY P. MINEAR ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. MINEAR",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has repeatedly held that the notice requirements of the Due Process Clause are satisfied by a method of notice that's reasonably calculated to provide interested parties with notice of the proceedings."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. MINEAR",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Court can certainly do that. We might caution that it's not necessary to do that in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Minear, the Third Circuit has apparently adopted a test that requires the Government to show a little more than that it dropped a notice in the mail, and that, in fact, the Government must show that procedures at the receiving facility, the prison, were reasonably calculated to deliver notice to the intended recipient."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that a -- a standard that the Government would find satisfactory?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. MINEAR",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We disagree with that, Your Honor, for the reasons set forth in Judge Alito's dissenting opinion on -- on that ground; namely, that it imposes burdens that are not necessary."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the Government have any special procedures for people in the military?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it's our position that ordinary mail is sufficient here as it would be in the wide variety of other cases, comparable other cases, this Court has addressed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Minear",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the year 2000, the Government, the DEA and the FBI, sent out roughly 9,000 notices of forfeiture to their incarcerated prisoners."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2001-00-6567",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3bd0aa3ba0b2b317f9cf73902198efdb1a4af16aff40dc56c5bf476a7c19755e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3bd0aa3ba0b2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Certified mail -- counsel suggests it could be above the constitutional minimum, but applying this Court's framework, this Court's test for assessing the adequacy of notice, we know it's not above the constitutional minimum because it will reduce the risk of erroneous deprivation at minimal burden, and we know it reduces the risk because it can only be -- the notice can only be delivered, if their signature is required, to the addressee."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
